{
  "$comment": "The canonical biped rig family (spec 107). PROVISIONAL: the bone contract, the sockets and the height are written down, but bindPose is null because no rig has been measured against it yet. Since spec 115 that is a state the pipeline can actually leave: exporting a job whose rig completed fills this in from the measured rig and keeps everything already decided here. Once filled in it is never rewritten -- a later unit of the family is checked against it instead, because the family's one clip library is what animates all of them. canonicalHeight is DEFAULT_CANONICAL_HEIGHT from src/units/canonical-height.ts: the height the renderer already draws a player at, (cow.metrics.headY 69 + headRadius 10.5) * PLAYER_FIGURE.bodyScale 0.7. World units, not metres -- a terrain chunk is 616 across. src/render/iso3d/world/unit-scale.test.ts asserts the three cannot drift apart.",
